WEBVTT

00:15:28.664 --> 00:15:30.013
(Laughs)

00:15:30.037 --> 00:15:33.240
And you can open up
your compassion in that.

00:15:33.748 --> 00:15:36.944
There's so many lessons in compassion
that can be found here.

00:15:36.968 --> 00:15:40.045
How about a general universal mercy
that we can all feel

00:15:40.069 --> 00:15:42.324
toward people who are
in solitary confinement.

00:15:42.348 --> 00:15:44.397
Let's have that be
part of the conversation.

00:15:44.421 --> 00:15:47.780
Now you've experienced it
for two days in your own house.

00:15:47.804 --> 00:15:49.869
Maybe it's time
to change the prison system?

00:15:49.893 --> 00:15:51.304
You see how hard this is.

00:15:51.328 --> 00:15:54.463
Or you can have compassion
toward people who have lost a loved one

00:15:54.487 --> 00:15:55.638
and they're alone.

00:15:55.662 --> 00:15:57.090
By feeling your own feelings,

00:15:57.114 --> 00:16:00.136
you can open up your feelings
more universally toward the world.